 }{9}\\le v\\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the image of the top side of $Δ$ under the action of $T?$" 13194139534887 17592186045417 false] [17592186389153 1074 "For our transformation $T,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.\n$$\n\nNotice that if we change $u$ to $r$ and $v$ to $\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich represents the usual formulas for changing from polar to Cartesian coordinates. \n\nTherefore, the pre-image $Δ$ of $D$ under the action of $T$ is the region that can be written as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le v\\le \\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is the rectangular region enclosed between\n\n- two vertical lines with Cartesian equations $u=1$ and $u=2,$ and\n\n- two horizontal lines with Cartesian equations $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{4},$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/88/88d58291666ed60113e3d16c5bc30e6d4375cbae3501f8e3e26bd9bbacb4940d.png)" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186389153 1074 "For our transformation $T,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.\n$$\n\nNotice that if we change $u$ to $r$ and $v$ to $\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich represents the usual formulas for changing from polar to Cartesian coordinates. \n\nTherefore, the pre-image $Δ$ of $D$ under the action of $T$ is the region that can be written as \n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le v\\le \\frac{5\\pi }{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis is the rectangular region enclosed between\n\n- two vertical lines with Cartesian equations $u=1$ and $u=2,$ and\n\n- two horizontal lines with Cartesian equations $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{4},$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/88/88d58291666ed60113e3d16c5bc30e6d4375cbae3501f8e3e26bd9bbacb4940d.png)" 13194139534887 17592186045417 false] [17592186442746 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442761 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442762 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442763 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442764 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442765 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1045 "Polar Coordinate Transformations" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1046 #edb/ref 17592186442762 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049321 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442746 1053 #uuid "5c82b827-3e4e-5f9f-9368-26da9d8bf53c" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442747 1080 "None of the statements are true" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442747 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442747 1083 #uuid "3d20667f-50b2-55b0-95fa-20f52b560b36" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442748 1080 "images/f3/f3425325c560606e15fc752f18e637f7ccab0eec8c973f022a4976b8477a7492.png" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442748 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442748 1083 #uuid "87b9e5b4-dff5-5eec-ba80-fedc99f32b46" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442749 1080 "images/40/40d60714c368f92bd7382005882c627be119f6cb05665441730887b60306cdb7.png" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442749 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442749 1083 #uuid "8c755e