deb933f" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442747 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442751 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442752 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442753 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442755 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442757 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442757 1077 "selection" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442757 1078 #edb/ref 17592186442755 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442757 1079 #uuid "8cd74140-69a0-5af3-8672-f40c3db56533" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442758 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442748 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442758 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442749 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442758 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442750 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442758 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442754 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442758 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442756 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442758 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442758 1077 "selection" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442758 1078 #edb/ref 17592186442749 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442758 1079 #uuid "e1fe8e38-4aad-57a4-8a8d-5a0d162037eb" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442759 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442758 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442759 1069 "q-160949" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442759 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442759 1071 "![](images/6b/6b0365b0f6b00859fb3739876f7d9a119db8b7f649e1935c66091285460e7f70.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane, shown above. The transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),\\,y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\n$$\n\nmaps the region $Δ$ from the $uv$-plane to $D.$ Which of the following could be the region $Δ?$" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442759 1072 #uuid "57a07fec-924e-51b2-9054-16b08d5b6be1" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442759 1074 "For our transformation $T,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.\n$$\n\nNotice that if we change $u$ to $r$ and $v$ to $\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich represents the usual formulas for changing from polar to Cartesian coordinates. \n\nTherefore, the pre-image $Δ$ of $D$ under the action of $T$ is the region that can be written as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is the rectangular region enclosed between\n\n- two vertical lines with Cartesian equations $u=0$ and $u=1,$ and\n\n- two horizontal lines with Cartesian equations $v=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/40/40d60714c368f92bd7382005882c627be119f6cb05665441730887b60306cdb7.png)" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442760 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442757 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442760 1069 "q-161034" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442760 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442760 1071 "![](images/b3/b3bef2dbb84cfe3a2881abf8f61761f98ea0d9cf4a07ea582355c57d375f975d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,3\\le u\\le 6,\\,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le v\\le \\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the top side of $Δ$ under the action of $T$ is a line segment. Which of the following statements are true regarding the image?\n\nI. The image makes the angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n\nII. The image makes the angle of $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n\nIII. The endpoints of the image lie on the circles of radii $3$ and $6$ centered at $O.$" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442760 1072 #uuid "6caf644a-b965-5b35-b048-eee4060c43c4" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442760 1074 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the top side.\n\nFor the top side, we have $v=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ and $3\\le u\\le 6.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})),\\,3\\le u\\le 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/b9/b976e62862ba82dfd89ff28627239dd5b5d1be1144e257223c091f29a5729f89.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the line that this segment lies on passes through the origin. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. The slope of the line is\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nAs a result, our line makes an angle of $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ radians with the positive $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\n- When $u=3,$ we obtain the point \n$(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}),\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})),$\nwhose distance to the origin is $3.$\n\n- When $u=6,$ we obtain the point \n$(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}),\\,6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})),$\nwhose distance to the origin is $6.$\n\nSo, the endpoints of the line segment lie on the circles of radii $3$ and $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442761 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442763 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442761 1062 #uuid "3e559c32-32ad-5b51-a713-cef4abf5f5ca" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442761 1063 #edb/ref 17592186278351 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442762 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442764 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442762 1062 #uuid "64d08072-1a49-5e0c-9af1-0ecfb9d8073a" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442762 1063 #edb/ref 17592186278344 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442763 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442765 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442763 1062 #uuid "9b9a8694-189b-58cf-bf5d-4a0e9eed87f4" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442763 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442760 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442764 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442761 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442764 1062 #uuid "d73744fd-8d46-5808-92e1-0ec7ee597069" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442764 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442759 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442765 1062 #uuid "d7f0238c-5d88-53fd-9153-3c953fcbb734" 13194139534887 17592186045417 true] [17592186442765 1063 #edb/ref 17592186389153 13194139534887 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-5c82b827-3e4e-5f9f-9368-26da9d8bf53c" 17592186442746 "answer-3d20667f-50b2-55b0-95fa-20f52b560b36" 17592186442747 "answer-87b9e5b4-dff5-5eec-ba80-fedc99f32b46" 17592186442748 "answer-8c755e5e-6783-571f-a88c-164c24a1dfcd" 17592186442749 "answer-98deceaf-7a7c-5395-80de-66909b2600ae" 17592186442750 "answer-9d738677-4b48-5272-ba62-6f070fe8babb" 17592186442751 "answer-a8188bf8-8b54-575b-933a-aa859ce24d7c" 17592186442752 "answer-d5079a63-2c21-5532-8a24-134a5b4af955" 17592186442753 "answer-da76ff9a-9c3b-5dcc-86dd-ebe90f5c27fb" 17592186442754 "answer-de7d22b9-d57c-5d7b-88cb-f0b4ca5f4a5d" 17592186442755 "a